== Modern Nutrition & Pharmacology

Composition, dry adzuki bean, approximate per 100 g raw — verify against USDA FoodData Central.

- Energy ~330 kcal; Water ~13 g
- Protein ~20 g
- Fat ~0.5 g
- Carbohydrate ~63 g; Dietary fiber ~13 g
- Folate ~620 µg (very high)
- Iron ~5 mg; Magnesium ~130 mg; Potassium ~1250 mg
- Anthocyanins (red seed coat) — modest
- Saponins, polyphenols

*Pharmacology of note:*
- *Diuretic / antiedema:* the classical 利水 action has modest preclinical support; the saponin fraction contributes.
- *Anti-inflammatory / antioxidant:* anthocyanins and polyphenols; preclinical.
- *Glycemic index:* low.
- *Hepatoprotective / nephroprotective:* preclinical evidence.
- *Cross-system convergence:* the Chinese 利水消腫 + Japanese folk-medical diuretic + modern preclinical diuretic-saponin evidence converges.

*Safe daily dosage / upper limit:* No toxicological upper limit. Routine cooked serving (~30–50 g raw / ~150–200 g cooked) is dietary register. Therapeutic decoction: 15–30 g dried beans. Risk groups: legume-allergy (rare); FODMAP-sensitive IBS.

